# .socraticodeignore — semantic-index exclusions (gitignore syntax).
# Layered on SocratiCode's built-in defaults + .gitignore.
#
# Vendored skill trees (managing-skills submodules) are not this project's
# code: they inflate embedding time and outrank first-party code in
# codebase_search results. See GH #182 / gregoryfoster/skills#76.
#
# NOTE: `skills/` is deliberately NOT excluded — this repo authors
# a first-party skill there (train-model/) alongside symlinks into
# skills-vendor/. The indexer does not follow
# symlinks, so excluding skills-vendor/ already drops the vendored content.
#
# `.skills/` holds the vendored copy of managing-skills' doctor.sh — same
# class of content, kept out for the same reason.
skills-vendor/
.claude/skills/
.skills/

# `docs/plans/` is dated design prose — AGENTS.md: "dated snapshots, never
# current guidance". It was 981 chunks, 36.6% of the code index and 2.3x all
# of src/, and it outranked first-party source on questions the plans answer
# wrongly: a context search for the validated_addresses status CHECK returned
# a plan showing 'assigned', a value migration 014 dropped and that
# SENSITIVE-AREAS.md calls a derived rollup, never a stored status.
#
# Same argument as skills-vendor/ above, applied to our own prose — which is
# worse, because ours is more plausible. Excluded from the CODE index only:
# the identical content stays embedded as the `design-plans` context
# artifact, so plan rationale is still searchable via codebase_context_search
# (deliberate call) rather than surfacing unbidden in codebase_search.
# See GH #218 (option A); the context-store share is still open there.
docs/plans/

# `docs/research/` is the other half of the same AGENTS.md sentence. Smaller
# (28 chunks, 1.0%) but identical in kind, and excluded on the identical
# terms: its one indexed file, address-validation-research.md, IS the
# `address-validation-research` context artifact, so nothing leaves the store.
# The ISO 19160 PDF beside it was never indexed (binary, unsupported
# extension) and is unaffected either way.
docs/research/

# --- Data, generated output and vendored specs (measured 2026-11-20, 1.14.0) ---
# Together 379 of the code index's 2,611 chunks (14.5%), none of it code an
# agent should be steered to. Each line was dry-run against the server's own
# getIndexableFiles: the 7 files below leave and nothing else moves.

# CRF training data: token-tagged <AddressString> XML. `upstream/labeled.xml`
# alone was 266 chunks (10.2%), more than half of all of src/ (502). It is
# rows, not prose or code; `grep` finds a labelled example exactly, and an
# embedding of 30 tagged addresses answers nothing. Each batch's rationale.md
# and manifest.json stay indexed: those are the first-party record.
training/**/*.xml

# This service's OpenAPI schema, generated from the app and drift-tested
# (#276). 29 chunks that restated models.py and outranked it: "validate
# endpoint response model fields and status enum" returned openapi.json's
# ValidationResult above the model's own definition. Still searchable where it
# belongs, as the `service-api-spec` context artifact (a single-file artifact
# is read verbatim and skips every ignore file).
/openapi.json

# Vendored USPS OpenAPI specs, 57 chunks. Third-party contracts, not our code,
# and both are context artifacts (`usps-api-spec`, `usps-enhanced-api-spec`),
# so nothing leaves the store. Same terms as docs/research/ above.
docs/usps-*.yaml

# Minified Tailwind build output (scripts/build/build-css.sh writes it from
# input.css + tailwind.config.js, which stay indexed). 11 chunks of utility
# classes on one 20 KB line.
src/address_validator/static/admin/css/tailwind.css

# --- Re-included: dropped by a built-in default, not by choice ---
# The built-in `build` pattern matches at any depth, so it took scripts/build/
# and its three first-party scripts (build-css.sh, download-tailwind.sh,
# pre-commit-tailwind.sh) with it. This file is read last, so a negation wins.
# scripts/build/bin/ (the downloaded tailwindcss binary) stays out: .gitignore
# names it, and the negation re-includes only the directory itself.
!scripts/build/

# NOT decided here: which extensions and dotfiles the walk admits is server env
# (EXTRA_EXTENSIONS, set for the infra/ units; INCLUDE_DOT_FILES, not set).
# See docs/SOCRATICODE.md -> "Beyond the built-in extensions".
